## 📝 Re-running the Script

To create these users again (if database is reset):

```bash
node scripts/register-test-users.mjs
```

The script will:
- Check if users already exist
- Create users if they don't exist
- Skip creation if they already exist (idempotent)

---

## 🔄 Reset Users

If you need to delete and recreate users:

```sql
-- Connect to your PostgreSQL database
-- Delete provider-related data first (foreign keys)
DELETE FROM "Subscription" WHERE "providerId" IN (
  SELECT id FROM "Provider" WHERE "userId" IN (
    SELECT id FROM "User" WHERE email IN ('admin@drivebook.com.au', 'instructor@drivebook.com.au')
  )
);

DELETE FROM "Provider" WHERE "userId" IN (
  SELECT id FROM "User" WHERE email IN ('admin@drivebook.com.au', 'instructor@drivebook.com.au')
);

-- Delete users
DELETE FROM "User" WHERE email IN ('admin@drivebook.com.au', 'instructor@drivebook.com.au');
```

Then re-run the script to create fresh users.

---

## 📊 Database IDs

**Created on:** First run (IDs will vary)

These IDs are generated dynamically using `cuid()` format.

To check current IDs:
```sql
SELECT id, email, role, "emailVerified" FROM "User" 
WHERE email IN ('admin@drivebook.com.au', 'instructor@drivebook.com.au');

SELECT p.id, p.name, p."approvalStatus", p."subscriptionTier", u.email 
FROM "Provider" p 
JOIN "User" u ON p."userId" = u.id 
WHERE u.email = 'instructor@drivebook.com.au';
```

